Subject: [PATCH 1/2] A view that holds still finishes its forest in one frame

The forest is placed one step per drawn frame (14 to 20 steps), a drawn frame takes the
software GL about 1.15 s on a busy machine (measured), so a view that held still after the
idle limit had its placement unfinished for some 20 s while the loop kept drawing a frame
per step, and 'no frame in 1.5 s' was true in the 2 to 3 s gaps between them. When the view
is held, the frame now pumps the placement to its end (the same trees as the steps give,
pinned) and a camera settle that was still waiting gets a frame and is placed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zPE7K49ycKieo7wJdrBFN
